From: Uke contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: uke: declare firmware quaternion endpoints

Declare three standard SSC firmware fusion datatypes without fitted chip or
calibration claims. Exact API and availability metadata still gates registration.
Preserve existing physical sensors, raw channels and Hall/ALS resource ownership.

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/uke-hardware.h
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/uke-hardware.h
@@ -108,6 +108,9 @@
 		UKE_SENSOR("sar", "Capacitive SAR", "sar", "SX937x"),
 		UKE_SENSOR("sensor-temperature", "Physical sensor temperature", "sensor_temperature", "LSM6DSO\0QMI8658"),
 		UKE_SENSOR("gravity", "Gravity and linear acceleration", "gravity", "SSC firmware fusion"),
+		UKE_SENSOR("rotation-vector", "ENU rotation vector", "rotv", "SSC firmware fusion"),
+		UKE_SENSOR("game-rotation-vector", "Relative rotation vector", "game_rv", "SSC firmware fusion"),
+		UKE_SENSOR("geomagnetic-rotation-vector", "Geomagnetic ENU rotation vector", "geomag_rv", "SSC firmware fusion"),
 #undef UKE_SENSOR
 	};
 	static const char *const cores[] = {
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/xiaomi,uke-ssc-sensors.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/xiaomi,uke-ssc-sensors.yaml
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
     description: Paired board lid input used to select the unoccluded ambient-light sensor.
 
 patternProperties:
-  '^(accelerometer|gyroscope|magnetometer|front-light|rear-light|color-temperature|proximity|flicker|sar|sensor-temperature|gravity)$':
+  '^(accelerometer|gyroscope|magnetometer|front-light|rear-light|color-temperature|proximity|flicker|sar|sensor-temperature|gravity|rotation-vector|game-rotation-vector|geomagnetic-rotation-vector)$':
     type: object
     properties:
       compatible:
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
       label: true
       qcom,ssc-datatype:
         $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
-        enum: [accel, gyro, mag, ambient_light, ambient_light_back, cct_front, proximity, flicker, sar, sensor_temperature, gravity]
+        enum: [accel, gyro, mag, ambient_light, ambient_light_back, cct_front, proximity, flicker, sar, sensor_temperature, gravity, rotv, game_rv, geomag_rv]
         description: SSC datatype used by the native discovery client.
       xiaomi,model-candidates:
         $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string-array
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-uke-ssc
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-uke-ssc
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
 Description:
                 Read-only count of supported sensor datatypes declared in the
-                controller's Device Tree, from 0 through 9. It does not identify
+                controller's Device Tree, from 0 through 12. It does not identify
                 fitted chips or establish physical sensor availability.
 
 What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_discovered_sensors
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
 Description:
                 Read-only count of declared sensors with an admitted SUID in
-                the current client generation, from 0 through 9. Zero is
+                the current client generation, from 0 through 12. Zero is
                 reported when the client is not current. No SUID is exposed.
 
 What:           /sys/devices/.../ssc_ready_sensors
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
 Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
 Description:
                 Read-only count of declared sensors with accepted metadata in
-                the current client generation, from 0 through 9. Zero is
+                the current client generation, from 0 through 12. Zero is
                 reported when the client is not current. This does not report
                 samples, calibration or physical accuracy.
 
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
 Description:
                 Read-only count of declared sensors whose IIO devices have
-                been registered, from 0 through 9. Registered devices may remain
+                been registered, from 0 through 12. Registered devices may remain
                 present after a service disappears, so this count alone does
                 not prove that samples are available.
 
